<programme start="20261019010000 +0000" stop="20261019040000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Florida State at Miami</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 3 Miami Hurricanes host the Florida State Seminoles in an ACC clash at Hard Rock Stadium. Miami leads the ACC with Darian Mensah&apos;s 1,438 passing yards and 15 touchdowns, while Ashton Daniels leads Florida State with 1,320 passing yards.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261019040000 +0000" stop="20261019070000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Utah at Colorado</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Colorado Buffaloes host the No. 11 Utah Utes in Week 7 at Folsom Field. Utah beat Kansas 41-24 to remain unbeaten at 5-0. Devon Dampier threw for 238 yards and 3 touchdowns. Colorado looks to bounce back after a tough stretch in Big 12 action.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261019070000 +0000" stop="20261019100000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Florida at Texas</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Texas Longhorns host Florida Gators in Week 7 at DKR-Texas Memorial Stadium. Texas lost 27-24 to Oklahoma after a last-play field goal, despite Arch Manning throwing 3 touchdown passes. Florida lost 38-19 to South Carolina in its last action.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261019100000 +0000" stop="20261019140000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">Unsportsmanlike with Evan, Canty and Michelle</title><desc lang="en">Start the day off right with Chris Canty, Evan Cohen and Michelle Smallmon providing an energizing and informative way to take on the day. Sports, life and laughter are what it&apos;s all about.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Talk Show</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25542634_b_v8_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261019140000 +0000" stop="20261019170000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Alabama at Tennessee</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 14 Tennessee Volunteers host the No. 6 Alabama Crimson Tide for the historic Third Saturday in October rivalry game. Alabama sits second in SEC with Keelon Russell leading the team, while Faizon Brandon leads Tennessee.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261019170000 +0000" stop="20261019200000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Notre Dame at BYU</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 8 Brigham Young Cougars host the No. 2 Notre Dame Fighting Irish in a clash of unbeatens at LaVell Edwards Stadium. Notre Dame beat Stanford, 58-7, as quarterback C.J. Carr threw three touchdown passes. Brigham Young beat Iowa State, 24-10.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
